WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.100
You have hundreds of contacts on LinkedIn.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.700
But you see them one by one, in an endless list sorted by date.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:15.900
Who do you know at Doctolib? Who could open the door to a job or a client? Impossible to tell at a glance.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.100
Synapses turns your list into a map of your network.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:27.500
To land an opportunity, grow your business, prepare a meeting, or expand your network where you’re missing contacts.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:34.500
First, request the full archive of your data in your LinkedIn settings. It arrives by email.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:42.100
Drop the archive as is onto Synapses: it’s read in your browser, and your network appears.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:51.100
Group your contacts however you like: by industry, company, function, seniority or connection year.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:01:01.100
Click an industry: see who you know there, at what level, and the people closest to you first.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:12.100
Pick a contact: you get their full profile. Your connection: your messages, your recommendations… and above all their colleagues at the same company.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:25.100
Targeting a company? Type its name: Synapses shows you who can open the door, from most senior to most junior.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:35.200
Group by company, with optional logos: see at a glance where your contacts cluster.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:39.600
And your file never leaves your browser.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:45.200
Synapses. Free, no sign-up. Finally see your network.
